{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014yTbAuVqjjdrrwjFKaWppo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel04.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel04.0 — ls core flag listing\"\n     3→release: rel04.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel04.0-uc001-ls\n     7→  - prd008-ls R1\n     8→  - prd008-ls R2\n     9→  - prd008-ls R3\n    10→  - prd008-ls R4\n    11→  - prd008-ls R5\n    12→  - prd008-ls R6\n    13→  - prd008-ls R7\n    14→\n    15→preconditions:\n    16→  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n    17→  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gls (coreutils).\n    18→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/ls/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    19→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    20→  - All differential tests use --color=never to eliminate ANSI escape variance (except color-specific structural tests).\n    21→  - For -l tests, the LsNormalizer replaces the mtime column with the placeholder MTIME before comparison.\n    22→  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/ls-fixture/) containing regular files of known sizes, a subdirectory, dotfiles, a symbolic link, and files with known permissions.\n    23→\n    24→test_cases:\n    25→  - name: ls_default_single_col_redirect\n    26→    description: 'No flags, stdout redirected (not a TTY); one entry per line in C locale order. stdout is a pipe (not TTY), so default format is single-column'\n    27→    inputs:\n    28→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    29→      stdin: null\n    30→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    31→    normalization: none\n    32→    expected:\n    33→      exit_code: 0\n    34→      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order, no dotfiles\n    35→      stderr: \"\"\n    36→    traces:\n    37→      - prd008-ls R1.2\n    38→      - prd008-ls R1.3\n    39→      - prd008-ls R1.4\n    40→\n    41→  - name: ls_default_multi_col_tty\n    42→    description: 'Default on TTY (or forced with -C and --width=80); multi-column output. -C forces multi-column even without TTY; -w 80 sets column width'\n    43→    inputs:\n    44→      args: [\"-C\", \"--color=never\", \"-w\", \"80\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    45→      stdin: null\n    46→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    47→    normalization: none\n    48→    expected:\n    49→      exit_code: 0\n    50→      stdout_structure: entries arranged in columns fitting within 80 characters\n    51→      stderr: \"\"\n    52→    traces:\n    53→      - prd008-ls R1.1\n    54→\n    55→  - name: ls_single_col_flag\n    56→    description: -1 forces single-column output regardless of TTY.\n    57→    inputs:\n    58→      args: [\"-1\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    59→      stdin: null\n    60→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    61→    normalization: none\n    62→    expected:\n    63→      exit_code: 0\n    64→      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order\n    65→      stderr: \"\"\n    66→    traces:\n    67→      - prd008-ls R2.1\n    68→\n    69→  - name: ls_long_format\n    70→    description: -l produces long format with permissions, nlink, owner, group, size, mtime, name.\n    71→    inputs:\n    72→      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    73→      stdin: null\n    74→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    75→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    76→    expected:\n    77→      exit_code: 0\n    78→      stdout_structure: |\n    79→        \"total N\" line followed by one long-format line per entry.\n    80→        Each line has: type+perms, nlink, owner, group, size, MTIME, name.\n    81→      stderr: \"\"\n    82→    traces:\n    83→      - prd008-ls R2.2\n    84→      - prd008-ls R2.3\n    85→      - prd008-ls R2.4\n    86→      - prd008-ls R2.5\n    87→      - prd008-ls R2.6\n    88→\n    89→  - name: ls_long_format_symlink\n    90→    description: -l on a directory containing a symlink shows \"name -> target\".\n    91→    inputs:\n    92→      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    93→      stdin: null\n    94→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    95→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    96→    expected:\n    97→      exit_code: 0\n    98→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \" -> \"'\n    99→      stderr: \"\"\n   100→    traces:\n   101→      - prd008-ls R2.6\n   102→\n   103→  - name: ls_long_human\n   104→    description: -lh displays human-readable file sizes matching gls -lh.\n   105→    inputs:\n   106→      args: [\"-lh\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   107→      stdin: null\n   108→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   109→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n   110→    expected:\n   111→      exit_code: 0\n   112→      stdout_structure: long format with sizes like \"1.0K\", \"1.5K\", \"1.0M\" instead of byte counts\n   113→      stderr: \"\"\n   114→    traces:\n   115→      - prd008-ls R5.1\n   116→      - prd008-ls R5.2\n   117→\n   118→  - name: ls_filter_all\n   119→    description: -a includes all entries including . and .. and dotfiles.\n   120→    inputs:\n   121→      args: [\"-a\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   122→      stdin: null\n   123→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   124→    normalization: none\n   125→    expected:\n   126→      exit_code: 0\n   127→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".\", \"..\", and \".hidden\"'\n   128→      stderr: \"\"\n   129→    traces:\n   130→      - prd008-ls R3.1\n   131→\n   132→  - name: ls_filter_almost_all\n   133→    description: -A includes dotfiles but excludes . and .. entries.\n   134→    inputs:\n   135→      args: [\"-A\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   136→      stdin: null\n   137→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   138→    normalization: none\n   139→    expected:\n   140→      exit_code: 0\n   141→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".hidden\" and must not contain standalone \".\" or \"..\" entries'\n   142→      stderr: \"\"\n   143→    traces:\n   144→      - prd008-ls R3.2\n   145→\n   146→  - name: ls_directory_itself\n   147→    description: -d shows the directory entry itself, not its contents.\n   148→    inputs:\n   149→      args: [\"-d\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   150→      stdin: null\n   151→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   152→    normalization: none\n   153→    expected:\n   154→      exit_code: 0\n   155→      stdout: \"testdata/ls-fixture/\\n\"\n   156→      stderr: \"\"\n   157→    traces:\n   158→      - prd008-ls R3.3\n   159→\n   160→  - name: ls_color_suppressed\n   161→    description: --color=never produces no ANSI escape sequences.\n   162→    inputs:\n   163→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   164→      stdin: null\n   165→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   166→    normalization: none\n   167→    expected:\n   168→      exit_code: 0\n   169→      stdout_structure: 'output must not contain \"\\\\033[\"'\n   170→      stderr: \"\"\n   171→    traces:\n   172→      - prd008-ls R4.4\n   173→\n   174→  - name: ls_color_always\n   175→    description: '--color=always produces ANSI escape sequences for file types. structural check only, not a diff test (ANSI codes must be present)'\n   176→    inputs:\n   177→      args: [\"--color=always\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   178→      stdin: null\n   179→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   180→    normalization: none\n   181→    expected:\n   182→      exit_code: 0\n   183→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"\\\\033[\"'\n   184→      stderr: \"\"\n   185→    traces:\n   186→      - prd008-ls R4.1\n   187→      - prd008-ls R4.3\n   188→\n   189→  - name: ls_missing_file\n   190→    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1, lists other args.\n   191→    inputs:\n   192→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"nonexistent\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   193→      stdin: null\n   194→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   195→    normalization: none\n   196→    expected:\n   197→      exit_code: 1\n   198→      stdout_structure: listing of testdata/ls-fixture/ entries\n   199→      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent\"\n   200→    traces:\n   201→      - prd008-ls R6.2\n   202→\n   203→  - name: ls_bad_option\n   204→    description: Unknown flag produces error and exits 2.\n   205→    inputs:\n   206→      args: [\"--invalid-flag\"]\n   207→      stdin: null\n   208→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   209→    normalization: none\n   210→    expected:\n   211→      exit_code: 2\n   212→      stderr_contains: \"unrecognized option\"\n   213→    traces:\n   214→      - prd008-ls R6.3\n   215→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d435111c-0cb8-4c04-97d5-71917f93f264","uuid":"81c5b369-eceb-4d90-9ab7-5aa09f16e206","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/243/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel04.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel04.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel04.0 — ls core flag listing\"\nrelease: rel04.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel04.0-uc001-ls\n  - prd008-ls R1\n  - prd008-ls R2\n  - prd008-ls R3\n  - prd008-ls R4\n  - prd008-ls R5\n  - prd008-ls R6\n  - prd008-ls R7\n\npreconditions:\n  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gls (coreutils).\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/ls/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - All differential tests use --color=never to eliminate ANSI escape variance (except color-specific structural tests).\n  - For -l tests, the LsNormalizer replaces the mtime column with the placeholder MTIME before comparison.\n  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/ls-fixture/) containing regular files of known sizes, a subdirectory, dotfiles, a symbolic link, and files with known permissions.\n\ntest_cases:\n  - name: ls_default_single_col_redirect\n    description: 'No flags, stdout redirected (not a TTY); one entry per line in C locale order. stdout is a pipe (not TTY), so default format is single-column'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order, no dotfiles\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R1.2\n      - prd008-ls R1.3\n      - prd008-ls R1.4\n\n  - name: ls_default_multi_col_tty\n    description: 'Default on TTY (or forced with -C and --width=80); multi-column output. -C forces multi-column even without TTY; -w 80 sets column width'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-C\", \"--color=never\", \"-w\", \"80\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: entries arranged in columns fitting within 80 characters\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R1.1\n\n  - name: ls_single_col_flag\n    description: -1 forces single-column output regardless of TTY.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-1\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R2.1\n\n  - name: ls_long_format\n    description: -l produces long format with permissions, nlink, owner, group, size, mtime, name.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: |\n        \"total N\" line followed by one long-format line per entry.\n        Each line has: type+perms, nlink, owner, group, size, MTIME, name.\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R2.2\n      - prd008-ls R2.3\n      - prd008-ls R2.4\n      - prd008-ls R2.5\n      - prd008-ls R2.6\n\n  - name: ls_long_format_symlink\n    description: -l on a directory containing a symlink shows \"name -> target\".\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output contains \" -> \"'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R2.6\n\n  - name: ls_long_human\n    description: -lh displays human-readable file sizes matching gls -lh.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-lh\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: long format with sizes like \"1.0K\", \"1.5K\", \"1.0M\" instead of byte counts\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R5.1\n      - prd008-ls R5.2\n\n  - name: ls_filter_all\n    description: -a includes all entries including . and .. and dotfiles.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-a\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".\", \"..\", and \".hidden\"'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R3.1\n\n  - name: ls_filter_almost_all\n    description: -A includes dotfiles but excludes . and .. entries.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-A\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".hidden\" and must not contain standalone \".\" or \"..\" entries'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R3.2\n\n  - name: ls_directory_itself\n    description: -d shows the directory entry itself, not its contents.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-d\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"testdata/ls-fixture/\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R3.3\n\n  - name: ls_color_suppressed\n    description: --color=never produces no ANSI escape sequences.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output must not contain \"\\\\033[\"'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R4.4\n\n  - name: ls_color_always\n    description: '--color=always produces ANSI escape sequences for file types. structural check only, not a diff test (ANSI codes must be present)'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--color=always\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: 'output contains \"\\\\033[\"'\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R4.1\n      - prd008-ls R4.3\n\n  - name: ls_missing_file\n    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1, lists other args.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--color=never\", \"nonexistent\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 1\n      stdout_structure: listing of testdata/ls-fixture/ entries\n      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R6.2\n\n  - name: ls_bad_option\n    description: Unknown flag produces error and exits 2.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--invalid-flag\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 2\n      stderr_contains: \"unrecognized option\"\n    traces:\n      - prd008-ls R6.3\n","numLines":215,"startLine":1,"totalLines":215}}}
